    <node id="Tomato">
      <data key="d0">Tomato</data>
      <data key="d1">food</data>
      <data key="d2">"A round to oval fruit that is typically red when ripe, used in various culinary applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"A round, red, pulpy fruit with a green stem, typically smooth and shiny."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spherical fruit, vibrant red color."</data>
      <data key="d3">"Can be sliced;"May be eaten raw or cooked;"used in cooking;can be diced;can be puréed;can be rinsed";can be sliced;cooked;eaten raw;used in salads or sauces.";used in sauces"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A";"rinsed_before_use"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"Center of the kitchen scene; lies on a countertop, positioned near a knife."&lt;SEP&gt;"Positioned on the right side of the dining table, near other items."&lt;SEP&gt;"Commonly found in kitchens or grocery stores; often on countertops during food preparation; found on cutting boards during slicing; placed in microwaves for heating."</data>
      <data key="d7">A ripe, red tomato is a spherical fruit known for its juiciness and vibrant color.&lt;SEP&gt;Tomato is a commonly used edible fruit in cooking, known for its versatile uses in salads, sauces, and various dishes.&lt;SEP&gt;A tomato is a fleshy fruit known for its juicy texture and rich flavor. It is commonly used in culinary dishes such as sauces and salads. The fruit can be sliced, diced, or puréed, and must be rinsed before preparation, particularly if consumed raw.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-30c39953c0d25d1f3c5e130739908d03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bcc15050b8adf34f86fc45460423efc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47e863c85da107c94adb93b1c1763edc</data>
